  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Barundi,Tuyage ! (Let&#x2019;s Talk, Burundi!)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Barundi, Tuyage ! (Let&#x2019;s Talk, Burundi!) project promotes dialogue about Burundi&#x2019;s history and strengthens social cohesion through community-based transitional justice. It fosters constructive discussions about past violence and encourages pluralistic narratives to create the foundations for mutual recognition and to tackle identity-based violence, with youth as the main target group. Diverse platforms consisting of community actions and new media are employed to stimulate dialogue, facilitate access to different viewpoints, provoke informed debates, and generate multiple narratives. Discussions take place simultaneously at the local, sub-national, and national levels as part of an interlinked strategy. Finally, the project supports communities to deal more constructively with the past and establish their own memory initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
